<title>FRANCE: Camdessus says dollar undergoing &quot;normalisation&quot;.</title>
<headline>Camdessus says dollar undergoing &quot;normalisation&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>International Monetary Fund (IMF) director Michel Camdessus said on Wednesday that the &quot;normalisation&quot; of the dollar reflected market belief in the strength of the U.S. economy.</p>
<p>&quot;This normalisation of the dollar is due essentially to the perception by the markets of the strength of the U.S. economy and against other major currencies,&quot; he told a hearing at the French Senate.</p>
<p>He also said current exchange rate levels were favourable to the world economy. &quot;We have never had a constellation so favourable to global economic development,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 42 21 53 81</p>
